    "---\n",
    "## 🧠 MASTER REFERENCE — Key Takeaways for Exams & Interviews\n",
    "\n",
    "### Architecture Decisions & Trade-offs\n",
    "\n",
    "| Decision | Why Made | Alternative | When to Use Alternative |\n",
    "|----------|----------|-------------|-------------------------|\n",
    "| BatchNorm after Conv | Stabilize training, faster convergence | LayerNorm, InstanceNorm | LayerNorm for transformers; InstanceNorm for style transfer |\n",
    "| MaxPool (not AvgPool) | Keeps strongest activations (texture) | AvgPool, Strided Conv | AvgPool for global feature aggregation; Strided Conv when learnable downsampling needed |\n",
    "| Adam optimizer | Fast convergence, adaptive LR | SGD + momentum | SGD often gives better final accuracy but needs careful tuning |\n",
    "| Pre-padding (not post) | LSTM final hidden state sees real content | Post-padding | Post-pad if using attention/packed sequences |\n",
    "| StandardScaler before PCA | Prevents scale-dominated components | MinMaxScaler | MinMaxScaler when features must be in [0,1] range |\n",
    "| PCA before t-SNE | Speed up t-SNE, remove noise | Direct t-SNE | Only if data is already low-dim (< 50 features) |\n",
    "| `c=class_labels` in scatter | Color by semantic meaning | `c=coordinates` | NEVER — coloring by coordinate tells you nothing |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Critical Exam Points\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **CNN receptive field grows** with depth: 1st layer sees 3×3, 2nd layer sees 5×5 (via the first layer), etc.\n",
    "2. **CrossEntropyLoss = Softmax + NLL**. Never apply softmax before it in the model.\n",
    "3. **PCA is linear, t-SNE is non-linear**. t-SNE distances are NOT meaningful — only cluster membership matters.\n",
    "4. **BiLSTM hidden state**: `h_n[-2]` = last forward layer, `h_n[-1]` = last backward layer.\n",
    "5. **ResNet skip connection**: `H(x) = F(x) + x`. If F(x)=0, layer becomes identity.\n",
    "6. **Feature extraction**: set `model.eval()` + `torch.no_grad()` — essential for correct results.\n",
    "7. **t-SNE perplexity**: related to number of neighbors (5–50 typical). Higher = more global structure.\n",
    "8. **Vanishing gradient** in deep RNNs/CNNs: solved by LSTM gates / ResNet skip connections respectively.\n",
    "9. **`model.train()` vs `model.eval()`**: controls Dropout (on/off) and BatchNorm (uses batch stats vs running stats).\n",
    "10. **Feature standardization**: always do BEFORE PCA. `scaler.fit()` on train, `scaler.transform()` on test.\n",
    "\n",
